module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Duality.CompactGeneration.SupportedQuasiCoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Duality.DerivedPushforward.DirectSums
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Modules.Colimits
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Modules.StalkAcyclic
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Triangulated.BrownRepresentability

/-!
# Direct sums in the derived category of complexes with support

Let `X` be a scheme and `T ⊆ X` a subset. Stacks 0A9A asserts that the strictly full, saturated,
triangulated subcategory `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X) ⊆ D(𝒪_X)` of complexes with quasi-coherent cohomology
supported on `T` is generated by a single perfect object, and "generated" there is read through
right-orthogonality, so the statement has content only in a model of the derived category whose
morphisms lie in the universe indexing the direct sums of `𝒪_X`-modules. This file supplies the
direct sums themselves: `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)` has `Type u`-indexed direct sums, and they are computed
in `D(𝒪_X)`.

The mechanism has two halves. The abstract half is
`Stacks.Duality.derivedCategoryB_isClosedUnderCoproducts`: a weak Serre subcategory `B` of a
Grothendieck abelian category that is closed under direct sums cuts out a subcategory of the
derived category that is closed under direct sums, because cohomology commutes with direct sums
there. The concrete half is that each of the two defining conditions is closed under direct sums.
For quasi-coherence that is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentColimits.isQuasicoherent_sigma`. For support it is the
statement proved here: taking stalks commutes with direct sums of sheaves of modules (Stacks
01AH), so a direct sum of sheaves whose stalks vanish off `T` again has vanishing stalks off `T`.

The weak Serre input for quasi-coherent modules on an *arbitrary* scheme,
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentWeakSerre.isQuasicoherent_isWeakSerre`, is also what makes
the triangulated structure on `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)` unconditional: in
`SupportedQuasiCoherent.lean` it is an explicit hypothesis of the general-scheme statements and
discharged only over an affine base, and that restriction is lifted here.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Duality.Supported.supportedModules_sigmaObj` — a direct sum of sheaves of `𝒪`-modules
  supported on `T` is supported on `T`.
* `Stacks.Duality.Supported.derivedSupported_isClosedUnderCoproducts` — `D_T(𝒪)` is closed under
  direct sums indexed by the Grothendieck universe.
* `Stacks.Duality.Supported.quasiCoherentSupported_isClosedUnderCoproducts` and
  `Stacks.Duality.Supported.hasCoproducts_quasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory` —
  `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)` is closed under direct sums, and has them.
* `Stacks.Duality.Supported.quasiCoherentSupported_isTriangulated` and its companions — the
  strictly full, saturated, triangulated structure on `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)`, for an arbitrary scheme
  and with no hypothesis.
* `Stacks.Duality.Supported.exists_isTriangulated_rightAdjoint_of_compactlyGenerated` — Brown
  representability ([Stacks, Tag 0A8G]) for `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)`, with every hypothesis other than
  compact generation discharged. Compact generation is Tag 0A9A together with Tag 0A9B.

## Implementation notes

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. Tag 0A9A has a single tagged statement, the existence of a
perfect generator, and that is not proved here: what is built is the direct-sum structure the
statement is phrased against. The tag's **affine case** — a perfect generator for
`D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})`, which is the base case of the induction the source runs — is proved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Duality/CompactGeneration/AffinePerfectGenerator.lean`, on
`Stacks.Duality.Supported.exists_isPerfect_quasiCoherentSupported_isWeakGenerator`; the
quasi-compact quasi-separated case, the statement of the tag, is the induction of Tag 08DR and is
`exists_isPerfect_quasiCoherentSupported_isWeakGenerator_of_qcqs` in the namespace
`Stacks.Duality.SupportedGeneration`, in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Duality/CompactGeneration/QcqsPerfectGenerator.lean`, which this
file does not import. Tag 08DT is the direct-sum statement for `D_QCoh` with no support condition,
and `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Duality/DerivedPushforward/DirectSums.lean` declines to tag it
as well, for the same reason — direct sums are produced only for index types of one universe rather
than for arbitrary index sets.

The index universe is the Grothendieck universe `u` of `𝒪_X`-modules. At the locally small model
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory` that is also the morphism universe of
`D(𝒪_X)`, so `HasCoproducts.{u}` is then exactly the hypothesis Brown representability
([Stacks, Tag 0A8G]) asks for; with `HasDerivedCategory.standard` the morphisms would live in
`Type (u + 1)` and the hypothesis would be false rather than unavailable. The derived category is
therefore left as an instance argument throughout, as in `SupportedQuasiCoherent.lean`, and never
pinned.

`Stacks.Duality.Supported.isClosedUnderColimitsOfShape_inf` is a general fact about object
properties with no derived category in it; it is stated here only because the file it belongs in,
`Mathlib/CategoryTheory/ObjectProperty/ColimitsOfShape.lean`, has the two one-sided instances and
not the meet. The same applies to
`Stacks.Duality.Supported.preservesColimitsOfShape_stalkAddCommGroupFunctor`, which belongs with
the rest of the stalk-colimit API in
`StacksFrontier/Topology/Sheaves/Modules/Colimits.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A9A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A9A)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08DT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08DT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01AH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01AH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A8G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A8G)
-/

-- This file uses the locally small derived-category models below, which are not
-- global instances (see `StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall`):
-- `D(R)` for sheaves of modules on a small site.
attribute [local instance] SheafOfModules.hasDerivedCategory

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty
  TopologicalSpace WeakSerre

universe w u

namespace Stacks.Duality.Supported

/-! ### Two general facts -/

/-- A meet of two properties of objects closed under colimits of shape `K` is closed under
colimits of shape `K`: a colimit presentation of an object by objects satisfying both properties
is a colimit presentation by objects satisfying each.

This belongs in `Mathlib/CategoryTheory/ObjectProperty/ColimitsOfShape.lean`, which has the
inverse-image and closure instances but not the meet. -/
theorem isClosedUnderColimitsOfShape_inf {C : Type*} [Category* C] (P Q : ObjectProperty C)
    (K : Type*) [Category* K] (hP : P.IsClosedUnderColimitsOfShape K)
    (hQ : Q.IsClosedUnderColimitsOfShape K) :
    (P ⊓ Q).IsClosedUnderColimitsOfShape K where
  colimitsOfShape_le _ := by
    rintro ⟨h⟩
    exact ⟨hP.colimitsOfShape_le _ ⟨h.ofLE fun _ hx => hx.1⟩,
      hQ.colimitsOfShape_le _ ⟨h.ofLE fun _ hx => hx.2⟩⟩

variable {X : TopCat.{u}} (𝒪 : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) RingCat.{u}) (T : Set X)

/-- **Taking stalks commutes with direct sums of sheaves of modules** (Stacks 01AH), in the
`AddCommGrpCat`-valued form. The `𝒪_x`-module-valued stalk functor preserves all colimits, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkFunctor_comp_forget₂` says that composing it with
`forget₂ (ModuleCat 𝒪_x) AddCommGrpCat` *is* the abelian-group-valued stalk functor.

This belongs with the rest of the stalk-colimit API in
`StacksFrontier/Topology/Sheaves/Modules/Colimits.lean`. -/
theorem preservesColimitsOfShape_stalkAddCommGroupFunctor (x : X) (J : Type u) :
    PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) (SheafOfModules.stalkAddCommGroupFunctor 𝒪 x) := by
  rw [← SheafOfModules.stalkFunctor_comp_forget₂]
  have := SheafOfModules.stalkFunctor_preservesColimits 𝒪 x
  infer_instance

/-! ### Direct sums of sheaves of modules with support -/

/-- **A direct sum of sheaves of `𝒪`-modules supported on `T` is supported on `T`.** The stalk at
a point `x ∉ T` of the direct sum is the direct sum of the stalks, each of which vanishes, and a
direct sum of zero objects is zero. -/
theorem supportedModules_sigmaObj {J : Type u} (M : J → SheafOfModules.{u} 𝒪)
    (hM : ∀ j, supportedModules 𝒪 T (M j)) : supportedModules 𝒪 T (∐ M) := by
  intro x hx
  have := preservesColimitsOfShape_stalkAddCommGroupFunctor 𝒪 x J
  refine IsZero.of_iso ?_
    (preservesColimitIso (SheafOfModules.stalkAddCommGroupFunctor 𝒪 x) (Discrete.functor M))
  exact IsColimit.isZero_pt (colimit.isColimit _) (Functor.isZero _ fun j => hM j.as x hx)

section Derived

variable [HasDerivedCategory.{w} (SheafOfModules.{u} 𝒪)]

/-- **`D_T(𝒪)` is closed under direct sums** indexed by any type of the Grothendieck universe:
cohomology commutes with direct sums in a Grothendieck abelian category, and the sheaves of
modules supported on `T` form a weak Serre subcategory closed under direct sums. -/
theorem derivedSupported_isClosedUnderCoproducts (J : Type u) :
    (derivedSupported 𝒪 T).IsClosedUnderColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) :=
  derivedCategoryB_isClosedUnderCoproducts _ _ (supportedModules_isWeakSerre 𝒪 T)
    (supportedModules_sigmaObj 𝒪 T)

end Derived

/-! ### `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_Z)` on an arbitrary scheme -/

section Scheme

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentColimits
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentWeakSerre

variable (Z : Scheme.{u}) (T : Set Z)
  [HasDerivedCategory.{w} (SheafOfModules.{u} Z.ringCatSheaf)]

/-- `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_Z)` is strictly full, for an arbitrary scheme: the weak Serre input for
quasi-coherent modules that `Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentSupported_isClosedUnderIsomorphisms`
carries as a hypothesis is available in general. -/
instance quasiCoherentSupported_isClosedUnderIsomorphisms :
    (quasiCoherentSupported Z T).IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms :=
  Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentSupported_isClosedUnderIsomorphisms Z T
    (isQuasicoherent_isWeakSerre Z)

/-- **`D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_Z)` is a triangulated subcategory of `D(𝒪_Z)`, for an arbitrary scheme.** It
is the meet of the subcategory cut out by quasi-coherence of the cohomology sheaves (Stacks 06VT)
and the one cut out by their support (Stacks 08DA), and both are weak Serre subcategories of the
`𝒪_Z`-modules. -/
instance quasiCoherentSupported_isTriangulated :
    (quasiCoherentSupported Z T).IsTriangulated :=
  Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentSupported_isTriangulated Z T (isQuasicoherent_isWeakSerre Z)

/-- **`D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_Z)` is saturated, for an arbitrary scheme**: a direct summand of a complex
with quasi-coherent cohomology supported on `T` is again one. -/
instance quasiCoherentSupported_isStableUnderRetracts :
    (quasiCoherentSupported Z T).IsStableUnderRetracts :=
  Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentSupported_isStableUnderRetracts Z T
    (isQuasicoherent_isWeakSerre Z)

/-- **`D_QCoh(𝒪_Z)` is closed under direct sums** indexed by any type of the Grothendieck
universe. This is [Stacks, Tag 08DT] phrased over `SheafOfModules.{u} Z.ringCatSheaf` and at an
arbitrary model of the derived category;
`Stacks.Duality.DerivedPushforward.derivedQuasicoherent_isClosedUnderCoproducts` is the same
statement phrased over `Z.Modules` at the locally small model, and the two are not
interchangeable because those types carry separately declared `Category` instances. -/
theorem derivedQuasiCoherent_isClosedUnderCoproducts (J : Type u) :
    (derivedQuasiCoherent Z).IsClosedUnderColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) :=
  derivedCategoryB_isClosedUnderCoproducts _ _ (isQuasicoherent_isWeakSerre Z)
    fun M hM =>
      have (j : J) : (M j).IsQuasicoherent := hM j
      isQuasicoherent_sigma M

/-- **`D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_Z)` is closed under direct sums** indexed by any type of the Grothendieck
universe: it is the meet of two subcategories that are. -/
theorem quasiCoherentSupported_isClosedUnderCoproducts (J : Type u) :
    (quasiCoherentSupported Z T).IsClosedUnderColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) :=
  isClosedUnderColimitsOfShape_inf _ _ _ (derivedQuasiCoherent_isClosedUnderCoproducts Z J)
    (derivedSupported_isClosedUnderCoproducts Z.ringCatSheaf T J)

/-- **`D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_Z)` has direct sums** indexed by any type of the Grothendieck universe, and
they are computed in `D(𝒪_Z)`. -/
instance hasColimitsOfShape_discrete_quasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory (J : Type u) :
    HasColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) (QuasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory Z T) :=
  have := Stacks.SmallDerivedCategory.hasColimitsOfShape_discrete_derivedCategory
    (SheafOfModules.{u} Z.ringCatSheaf) J
  have := quasiCoherentSupported_isClosedUnderCoproducts Z T J
  inferInstance

/-- `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_Z)` has all direct sums indexed by the Grothendieck universe of
`𝒪_Z`-modules. At the locally small model that universe is also the morphism universe of
`D(𝒪_Z)`, so this is the direct-sum hypothesis of Brown representability
([Stacks, Tag 0A8G]). -/
theorem hasCoproducts_quasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory :
    HasCoproducts.{u} (QuasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory Z T) := fun J =>
  hasColimitsOfShape_discrete_quasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory Z T J

end Scheme

/-! ### Brown representability for `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_Z)` -/

section BrownRepresentability

open CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated Opposite

/-- **Brown representability for `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_Z)`** ([Stacks, Tag 0A8G]). Let `Z` be a scheme,
`T ⊆ Z` a subset and `F : D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_Z) ⥤ D` an exact functor of triangulated categories which
preserves direct sums. If `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_Z)` is compactly generated by a family `E` — each
`preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op (E i))` preserves direct sums, and the only objects right orthogonal
to all shifts of all `E i` are the zero objects — then `F` has a right adjoint, which is again
exact.

**Of the hypotheses of Tag 0A8G, all but compact generation are discharged by instance search
here**, which is the point of the file: `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_Z)` is a strictly full triangulated
subcategory of `D(𝒪_Z)` by `quasiCoherentSupported_isTriangulated`, it is locally small in `u`
because the derived category in force is the locally small one, and it has the `Type u`-indexed
direct sums by `hasCoproducts_quasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory` — `Type u` being also its
morphism universe, which is what Tag 0A8G needs and what
`CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard` would not give.

The remaining hypothesis, a compact generating family, is exactly the content of [Stacks, Tag
0A9A] (a single perfect generator) together with [Stacks, Tag 0A9B] (a perfect object of
`D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_Z)` is compact). Both hold for `Z` quasi-compact and quasi-separated and `T` closed
with quasi-compact complement
(`Stacks.Duality.Supported.exists_isCompactObject_isPerfect_isWeakTriangulatedGenerator` and
`Stacks.Duality.Supported.isCompactObject_iff_isPerfect`, in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Duality/CompactGeneration/SupportedCompactPerfect.lean`), which
imports this file; the statement here is the general mechanism, for an arbitrary scheme `Z`, and
no `@[stacks]` attribute is attached.

This is the supported analogue of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_isTriangulated_rightAdjoint_of_compactlyGenerated`,
which is the same statement for `D(𝒪_Z)` itself. -/
theorem exists_isTriangulated_rightAdjoint_of_compactlyGenerated (Z : Scheme.{u}) (T : Set Z)
    {D : Type (u + 1)} [Category.{u} D] [HasZeroObject D] [Preadditive D] [HasShift D ℤ]
    [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D]
    (F : QuasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory Z T ⥤ D)
    [F.CommShift ℤ] [F.IsTriangulated]
    [∀ α : Type u, PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete α) F]
    {ι : Type u} (E : ι → QuasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory Z T)
    [∀ (i : ι) (α : Type u),
      PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete α) (preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op (E i)))]
    (hE : ∀ K : QuasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory Z T,
      ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal K → IsZero K) :
    ∃ (G : D ⥤ QuasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory Z T) (adj : F ⊣ G) (_ : G.CommShift ℤ),
      adj.IsTriangulated :=
  have := hasCoproducts_quasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory Z T
  Pretriangulated.exists_isTriangulated_rightAdjoint_of_compactlyGenerated F E hE

end BrownRepresentability

end Stacks.Duality.Supported

end
